# LUCI social media

Canonical strategy (Jane): **`LUCI Systems Design System/ui_kits/content-marketing/social-media-strategy.html`**. Mike-facing one-pager: **`social-media-overview-for-mike.html`** (cadence, platform, rules, post types only).

## Channel & cadence

- **LinkedIn, company page only** (Phase 1). Mike's personal page is a later phase, not now.
- **2–3 posts per week.** Consistency beats volume. If the bench is empty, post twice — never manufacture a third to hit a quota.
- Default weekly rhythm: **Tue** = weekly series · **Wed** = field or case study · **Thu** = thought leadership or news (conditional third post).

## Friday prep (the standing weekly process)

**Trigger phrases:** "prep next week's posts" · "Friday social prep" · "prep social for next week" · "build the week's batch".

Every Friday, Jane + Cursor prep the **following** week's 2–3 posts so they are draft-ready before Monday. Nothing posts without Mike's later sign-off.

### What Jane does Friday

1. Opens chat and says the trigger phrase (optionally names the posting week, e.g. "week of Jul 27").
2. **If she has field media:** drops progress photos / videos into `ui_kits/content-marketing/social-intake/<YYYY-MM-DD>/` (date = Friday of prep, or the Monday of the posting week — use the folder Jane creates or the agent creates) **or** attaches them in chat. Notes any client/anonymization sensitivities.
3. **If she has no media:** says so — the agent searches existing LUCI content and proposes a bench of options.

### What the agent does Friday (always, in this order)

1. **Inventory media** (if any): list every file, note duration/orientation/identifiable content risks, propose 2–3 engagement treatments per strong asset (crop, cut points, before/after pair, silent reel, still-from-video, diagram overlay, etc.).
2. **Edit media when asked / when the treatment is clear:** use `ffmpeg` for cuts, crops, mute, still extraction, simple assemblies; HyperFrames only when a branded motion lockup is needed. Write outputs into the same week's `social-intake/<week>/exports/`. Never invent client names or leave identifiable signage in exports.
3. **Propose the week's 3-slot batch:**
   - **Slot A — Weekly series (Tue):** one post in the locked series format. If format is still pending, propose options and ask Jane to lock before drafting copy. Series runs a fixed 8–10 week season (not indefinite) — see series timetable in the strategy.
   - **Slot B — Field / case (Wed):** prefer Jane's uploaded progress media → client in-the-field post. If no media, pull from case-study snippets, diagram-led posts, or existing approved photography.
   - **Slot C — Third post (Thu):** thought leadership (Mike / mined insights), case-study snippet, or industry/partner news (lowest priority; apply news guardrails). Prefer Mike-forward when the bench allows.
4. **No-media fallback:** search strategically across Content Lab (`index.html`, `sources/`), mined insights, case studies, canonical diagrams (`assets/diagrams/`), sales/capabilities visuals, and prior approved field photos. Surface 3–5 options with rationale; Jane picks; then draft.
5. **Draft into Social Studio templates**, then assemble into **`social-this-week.html`** for Jane's review in the Preview Hub. Do **not** re-add to `review-queue.json` / deploy to IMP until Jane says the batch is ready for Mike.

### After Friday

- Jane self-reviews (anonymization, competitor screen, voice flags).
- When she says the batch is ready for Mike: re-add `social-this-week` to `review-queue.json`, `npm run deploy:portal`, tell her the IMP URL + hard-refresh.
- Mike reviews the batch once; Jane posts Tue / Wed / Thu of the posting week.

## The five post types

Every post is one of: (1) client in-the-field, (2) case study / snippet, (3) thought leadership (Mike), (4) industry / partner news, (5) the weekly series. If a draft doesn't clearly fit one, cut it or reframe it.

## Messaging discipline (the one rule the visuals fight)

- **LED walls, racks, before/after, process video = the hook, never the headline.** The caption always closes on the abstraction: one interface, one team, one accountable system.
- **Every post routes to one of the four pillars** (01 visibility/control, 02 align teams, 03 activate guest experience, 04 A/V that scales & improves). No pillar, no post.
- **Prefer diagram-led posts** when the goal is the abstraction. Canonical diagrams (What LUCI is, Consolidation ledger, System architecture, Embedded Operation orbit) are available and on-brand.
- **Write for the person running the property, not the person racking the gear.** Audience is IT and operations leadership (Dir/VP/C-suite), not A/V technicians.

## Anonymization & client rules (hard)

- **No client names on in-the-field posts.** No property-identifiable signage, uniforms, or landmarks.
- **State it's a work in progress, not a finished project.** Promise the finalized view; keep a placeholder for the reveal post.
- **Named case study or named video only with the client's OK on file.** Unnamed video is fine.
- **No timelines, scope, pricing, or go-live claims** in field posts.
- **No % boasts or unverified metrics** in brand copy (proof rules from Messaging Guide).

## Sign-off workflow (weekly batch) — nothing posts without Mike's OK

1. **Friday before:** Jane + Cursor run Friday prep — media inventory/edits, 3-slot batch drafted in Social Studio templates, assembled into **`social-this-week.html`** (Preview Hub only).
2. Jane self-reviews: anonymization, competitor screen, voice flags. Fix or cut before Mike sees it.
3. When Jane says the batch is ready for Mike: re-add `social-this-week` to `review-queue.json`, rebuild, `npm run deploy:portal`. Do **not** re-add until she says so.
4. Mike reviews the one page, one sitting, comments or approves the batch (ideally before the Tuesday post).
5. Jane applies comments. If Mike kills a post, it's killed — no revival. His edit wins.
6. Jane posts the approved batch to LinkedIn manually (Tue / Wed / Thu); marks each Live in the Content Lab; parks the queue item again until the next batch.

**Loosening the gate:** after ~8–10 clean batches, revisit. The weekly series and approved-format snippets may move to a lighter heads-up batch. **Client-in-field and first-person Mike copy stay gated indefinitely.** Mike decides when, not us.

## News guardrails

- **Commentary, not re-share.** Add a LUCI point of view on top, or don't post.
- **No competitor promotion.** When in doubt, don't post — downside is asymmetric.
- **Partner news only when the integration is already public.** Pre-announcement = wait, no exceptions, even indirectly.
- **Honesty Protocol.** Credit partners/backends by name. Never imply LUCI owns native zone logic or routing that belongs to a third party (e.g. Q-SYS).

## Voice (short — full canon in `luci-messaging-voice.mdc` + Messaging Guide)

- **Always A/V** — never "AV" or "A-V" — in body, captions, alt text, hashtags, and on visuals.
- **Never "layer" as a noun for LUCI.** Use *orchestration engine* / *LUCI orchestrates…*.
- **Describe what the platform does, not how it feels.** "Operate every endpoint from one interface" passes; "absurdly simple" does not.
- **Watch repetition** of *engine* / *orchestrates* in a short caption — rotate to a precise alternative.
- **Institutions, not adjectives.** Declarative, subtraction framing.

## Where the work happens

- **Content Lab** (`index.html`) — input side: sources, mined ideas, voice flags.
- **Social Studio** (`social-studio.html`) — drafting workspace, one template per post type; Friday prep starts here.
- **This week's posts** (`social-this-week.html`) — clean Mike-facing review page; parked from IMP until Jane says a batch is ready.
- **Social intake** (`social-intake/<week>/`) — Friday drop folder for raw progress photos/videos + `exports/` cuts.
- **Transcript miner** (`scripts/mine-transcripts.mjs`) — surfaces candidate insights from past Cursor transcripts and OneDrive call recordings.

## Weekly series — locked (Season 1)

**Format:** **Control the Whole Property** (evolved from “What LUCI Controls”).
**Slot:** Tuesday weekly series post.
**Length:** 8–10 week season, then two-week pause.
**Medium:** **30-second video** per week. **All visuals AI-generated** (map, zone footage, detail shots) — no stock, no required client B-roll. Per-episode Claude prompts in `social-intake/control-the-whole-property/` include per-shot AI generation prompts + assembly spec.

Season 1 order (default): **series intro (Ep01)** → casino floor → sportsbook → pool deck & cabanas → bingo hall → event & banquet → F&B → hotel lobby → conference rooms → marketing signage vs guest TVs → full-property map finale.

Caption closes on one interface / one map — zone is the hook, not the headline.
